  "name": "Question 14",
  "problem": "In a sports warehouse, a large container contains several thousand baseballs. According to a report from the manufacturer, $10%$ of these balls are defective. \n\nA random sample of size $n=20$ is taken from the container. What is the mean and variance of $\\overset{^}{\\,p},$ the proportion of defective balls in the sample?\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the number of baseballs in the box is significantly larger than the number in the sample.*",
